---
/**
 * Page-specific (how-it-works): the four filing steps as a numbered rail, so
 * "only one step spends the model" is visible before a word is read. Steps 1,
 * 3, 4 are neutral code steps, step 2 is the single accent-filled model step
 * with a paid tag and a small fan-out glyph (one source, several notes).
 * All step facts are kept in full. Markup is written out per step (not a data
 * array) so inline code spans stay real elements. Filled surfaces, no border
 * boxes. Scoped CSS, theme-aware via Starlight tokens.
 */
---

<ol class="rail">
  <li class="step">
    <span class="n" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
    <div class="card">
      <div class="head">
        <span class="title">Copy</span>
        <span class="who code">code</span>
      </div>
      <p class="body">
        The source goes into <code>raw/</code> untouched, hashed, with the obvious
        structure pulled out. Free.
      </p>
    </div>
  </li>
  <li class="step paid">
    <span class="n" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
    <div class="card">
      <div class="head">
        <span class="title">Understand</span>
        <span class="who model">model</span>
        <span class="paidtag">the only paid step</span>
      </div>
      <div class="paidrow">
        <p class="body">
          For each thing in the source: pick its type and folder, write a one-line
          summary, pull out the decisions and actions, and tag it with the words you
          will search for later, even if the source never used them. A dense source
          fans out into several small notes.
        </p>
        <svg class="fan" viewBox="0 0 92 56" aria-hidden="true">
          <rect class="src" x="2" y="21" width="20" height="14" rx="3.5"></rect>
          <path class="wire" d="M24 28 C 40 28, 44 9, 62 9"></path>
          <path class="wire" d="M24 28 L 62 28"></path>
          <path class="wire" d="M24 28 C 40 28, 44 47, 62 47"></path>
          <rect class="out" x="64" y="2" width="20" height="14" rx="3.5"></rect>
          <rect class="out" x="64" y="21" width="20" height="14" rx="3.5"></rect>
          <rect class="out" x="64" y="40" width="20" height="14" rx="3.5"></rect>
        </svg>
      </div>
    </div>
  </li>
  <li class="step">
    <span class="n" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
    <div class="card">
      <div class="head">
        <span class="title">File</span>
        <span class="who code">code</span>
      </div>
      <p class="body">
        Look up people by name and alias, flag anything unresolved for review, and
        write the note without ever overwriting an existing one. Merging a renamed
        person into their old note is the model's call, made back in step 2.
      </p>
    </div>
  </li>
  <li class="step">
    <span class="n" aria-hidden="true">4</span>
    <div class="card">
      <div class="head">
        <span class="title">Tidy</span>
        <span class="who code">code</span>
      </div>
      <p class="body">
        <code>check</code> rebuilds the index and flags broken links, topic and event
        notes that link to no person, organization, or thing, and any note with no
        tags. It never blocks and never silently drops anything.
      </p>
    </div>
  </li>
</ol>

<style>
  .rail {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.55rem;
  }
  .step {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2rem 1fr;
    gap: 0.7rem;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }
  /* Starlight owl-spacing leaks margin-top onto later grid children */
  .rail > .step,
  .step > * {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .n {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 2rem;
    height: 2rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-1);
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--sl-color-gray-3) 22%, var(--sl-color-bg));
  }
  .step.paid .n {
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--sl-color-text-accent) 18%, var(--sl-color-bg));
  }
  .card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.35rem;
    padding: 0.85rem 1rem;
    border-radius: 13px;
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--sl-color-gray-3) 10%, var(--sl-color-bg));
  }
  .step.paid .card {
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--sl-color-text-accent) 12%, var(--sl-color-bg));
  }
  .head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.25rem 0.55rem;
  }
  .title {
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
  }
  .who {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--sl-font);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    padding: 0.1rem 0.5rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
  }
  .who.code {
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-1);
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--sl-color-gray-3) 34%, var(--sl-color-bg));
  }
  .who.model {
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--sl-color-text-accent) 20%, var(--sl-color-bg));
  }
  .paidtag {
    font-family: var(--sl-font);
    font-size: 0.66rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
  }
  .body {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-1);
  }
  .body code {
    font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
    font-size: 0.83rem;
    padding: 0.08rem 0.35rem;
    border-radius: 6px;
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--sl-color-gray-3) 25%, var(--sl-color-bg));
  }
  .paidrow {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1.1rem;
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .paidrow .body {
    flex: 1 1 auto;
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .fan {
    flex: 0 0 92px;
    width: 92px;
    height: 56px;
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .fan .src {
    fill: color-mix(in oklab, var(--sl-color-gray-2) 45%, var(--sl-color-bg));
  }
  .fan .out {
    fill: color-mix(in oklab, var(--sl-color-text-accent) 42%, var(--sl-color-bg));
  }
  .fan .wire {
    fill: none;
    stroke: color-mix(in oklab, var(--sl-color-text-accent) 55%, transparent);
    stroke-width: 1.6;
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .fan {
      display: none;
    }
  }
</style>
